WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.769 --> 00:00:01.772
(Audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:01.772 --> 00:00:02.605
Well, it's Thanksgiving week

00:00:02.605 --> 00:00:05.700
and we're always thankful
when our first guest stops by.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.350
That's why we're calling this whole hour,

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.607
'Gratitude with Garth.'

00:00:09.617 --> 00:00:12.139
(Audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:12.139 --> 00:00:13.440
He's the only artist in music history

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.890
to have nine albums to
be certified Diamond,

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.320
which means they each sold
over 10 million units.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.090
Just in case you're wondering at home,

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:25.800
most artists have like one
album that might sell that much

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.720
and he's got nine.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.030
His latest album is
called 'Time Traveler.'

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.110
It's available as part

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.720
of the limited series seven disc box set.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.230
You can find it exclusively
at a Bass Pro shop near you

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.670
don't, man, if you go
there, you're gonna end up

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.920
with 50,000 things you
didn't know you want.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.230
It's like Target, it's,
but it's a great store.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.370
But you end up with everything

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:47.042
and you're like, I'm
totally gonna go fishing.

00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:47.875
(audience laughing)

00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:49.540
Everybody give it up for Garth Brooks.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:50.373
(Audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:50.373 --> 00:00:54.040
(band playing upbeat music)

00:01:22.499 --> 00:01:27.499
- [Garth and Kelly] (indistinct chatter)

00:01:27.661 --> 00:01:31.911
(Audience cheering and applauding)

00:01:33.838 --> 00:01:35.070
- But happy Thanksgiving by the way.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.122
- Thank you very much.

00:01:36.122 --> 00:01:37.534
I'm gonna put gut hider on.

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:38.367
I love it.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:39.361
(laughing)

00:01:39.361 --> 00:01:40.753
- Thank you very much.

00:01:40.753 --> 00:01:42.459
- (laughing) Woo, now I can gonna relax.

00:01:42.459 --> 00:01:44.603
- Now it's, now it's out. That's it.

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:45.436
I love you right now.

00:01:45.436 --> 00:01:46.269
(laughing)

00:01:46.269 --> 00:01:47.935
Well wait. This is, all of this is we're,

00:01:47.935 --> 00:01:48.930
it's like we're related,
but, so wait, what?

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.430
Today is all about gratitude,

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:51.660
which I think is perfect for you.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.940
We were trying to find, 'cause
we love you on this show

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.140
we've had you on and we're, what can we do

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.460
that's like different and special?

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:57.630
And Thanksgiving was this week

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.570
and you are such a giving person,

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:02.520
but I think that you're
also always in a state

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.040
of like gratitude for everything
as well, which is cool.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.540
'cause you recognize all the blessings.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:07.373
- Yeah amen.

00:02:07.373 --> 00:02:08.970
Well, you, you're that same way.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:10.830
- I am but you're like the next degree.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.210
We've talked about
this, me and my friends.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.116
- Really ?

00:02:13.116 --> 00:02:14.782
Yeah. They, everybody
thought I was like this

00:02:14.782 --> 00:02:17.340
and then they, you were
introduced in their life

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.800
and they're like, oh no,
you don't even count.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.330
But what does this, what does it mean

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.070
to like be grateful,
especially around Thanksgiving?

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:23.903
Like what do you do?

00:02:23.903 --> 00:02:25.440
You go big for Thanksgiving, your family?

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.270
- Yeah, well, when
you're married to, well,

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.560
one of the greatest cooks on the planet.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.393
- Oh my God.

00:02:29.393 --> 00:02:30.226
Don't brag about it.

00:02:30.226 --> 00:02:31.500
- Well, I won't, we'll talk about

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.580
how great of a singer she is.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.172
- I know.

00:02:34.172 --> 00:02:35.022
- And then we'll talk about that.

00:02:35.022 --> 00:02:36.030
That's probably five and six on our list

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.203
of top 10 things to do.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.380
But she, I think it's fun.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:43.320
My thing is this and, and you
guys might feel the same way

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.580
when it comes to the future.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:45.780
You know, I think it's what you're

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:47.790
just grateful for is just one more day.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.012
Right, of getting to do this.

00:02:50.012 --> 00:02:50.845
So I think that's it.

00:02:50.845 --> 00:02:54.310
Just truthfully, if I could
say, what I'd love to say is

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.330
the day I take my last
breath on this planet,

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.070
I'd love for my three
girls to be around me.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.854
And I love for the Queen to be around me,

00:03:01.854 --> 00:03:04.650
but for as far as Miss
Yearwood, I don't know.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:05.580
You know, I've said this before.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:06.780
I found her in the past life.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.571
I'll find her in the next.

00:03:08.571 --> 00:03:10.643
She just, it's just I....

00:03:10.643 --> 00:03:12.243
- Well have a great day everybody.

00:03:12.243 --> 00:03:14.250
(Audience cheering and applauding)

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.441
- She makes it fun, you know?

00:03:16.441 --> 00:03:17.523
She makes it really fun.

00:03:17.523 --> 00:03:18.356
Don't cry at lunch, Garth.

00:03:18.356 --> 00:03:19.189
Okay.

00:03:19.189 --> 00:03:20.730
So it's amazing though.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:23.250
It's such a beautiful love
between the two of you.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.560
It is. And you are tearing up
and you're making me tear up

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.212
and my makeup artist is gonna kill me.

00:03:27.212 --> 00:03:28.290
- I'm not tearing up.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:29.130
- Yeah, you are.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:29.963
Yeah, you are.

00:03:29.963 --> 00:03:31.290
I love it.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.690
So wait, so why time traveler?

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:34.890
Why the title of that?

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:37.140
- Well, you know, country music as well,

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:38.310
if not better than everybody.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:40.080
And country music just stays sincere.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.160
It does its thing, but

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.672
through the decades sometimes
it gets dressed up different.

00:03:44.672 --> 00:03:45.900
And I swear you could
take two of these cuts

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.180
and you could play 'em in the
seventies. They would fit.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:49.013
- I love it.

00:03:49.013 --> 00:03:49.846
- You could take a couple of these cuts.

00:03:49.846 --> 00:03:51.512
It'd be in the nineties. I
mean, that's kind of where,

00:03:51.512 --> 00:03:52.983
you know, where our stuff was born.

00:03:53.893 --> 00:03:54.900
And then the stuff that'll just go right

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.854
along with today's stuff.

00:03:56.854 --> 00:03:58.110
So that's what I love about country music.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:00.360
As much as you might dress it
different through the decades,

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.220
it still stays true to itself.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.050
And so Time Traveler just seemed to pass

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:05.940
through all those eras of country music.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.020
- Yeah, it's a cool title.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.300
Well, in celebration of
Thanksgiving this week,

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.654
we are doing a little
'Gratitude with Garth' y'all

00:04:11.654 --> 00:04:14.820
(upbeat music)
(Audience cheering)

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.620
Grateful for where you came from, right?

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:17.453
This is like something

00:04:17.453 --> 00:04:18.690
that you always talk about, right?

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:19.523
- Amen.

00:04:19.523 --> 00:04:20.437
- Yeah, me too.

00:04:20.437 --> 00:04:21.960
- It's, it's, you're grateful
for where you're from

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.180
and you're grateful that you

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:25.440
kind of ended up where you're at.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:27.120
If that makes any sense.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.490
And people go, 'Hey, would you
change anything in the past?'

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.650
And you go, not if it
would change one thing

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:33.312
of where I'm at right now, right?

00:04:33.312 --> 00:04:34.382
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:34.382 --> 00:04:37.592
(Audience cheering)
- That's the thing.

00:04:37.592 --> 00:04:38.425
- Yeah.

00:04:38.425 --> 00:04:40.091
Even the bad stuff. Oh, even
the stuff that's not great

00:04:40.091 --> 00:04:41.757
- Is the bad stuff bad?
I mean, here's the thing.

00:04:41.757 --> 00:04:42.590
- Sometimes,

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:43.423
- So we talk about marriage sometimes

00:04:43.423 --> 00:04:44.640
and sometimes marriage doesn't work out,

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:47.820
but the children you have,
they're the perfect mix

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.740
of whoever you, and maybe you
didn't get along with 'em,

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:51.600
but those kids would have to be different.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.270
If you just love 'em the
way they are, it's well,

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.523
sometimes the way they are.

00:04:55.523 --> 00:04:57.189
(Audience laughing) But
you know what I'm mean.

00:04:57.189 --> 00:04:58.022
- No, wait, okay, so explain,

00:04:58.022 --> 00:05:00.480
this is the third limited
series box set, right?

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.280
So explain why and why Bass Pro Shop.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.170
I love Bass Pro Shop, but man, you go in

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.180
that place, it's like Target.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:08.280
You go out with things you don't need,

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.450
but you love.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:11.820
- Well you don't know you need them yet,

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:12.653
- Do you?

00:05:12.653 --> 00:05:14.171
Okay, okay.

00:05:14.171 --> 00:05:15.004
- You'll, you'll get there.

00:05:15.004 --> 00:05:15.837
- Okay.

00:05:15.837 --> 00:05:16.670
So not enough time,

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.731
but why, why, why this?

00:05:18.731 --> 00:05:19.564
- Well, it is really cool.

00:05:19.564 --> 00:05:21.180
So before you were born, we did the first

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.280
limited series, right?

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:23.113
(Audience laughing)

00:05:23.113 --> 00:05:23.946
- No.

00:05:23.946 --> 00:05:24.960
- So in the nineties
we did a limited series

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:28.050
and then in 2008 we did
a second limited series.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:29.160
And now this is our last one.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.420
And what it does is it allows you

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:32.250
to catch up on the past music

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:33.600
without having to pay for all of them.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.120
So you kind of do hopefully a small price

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.470
for this, perfect for Christmas.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.303
- Like a bundle

00:05:38.303 --> 00:05:39.136
- Kind of stuff.

00:05:39.136 --> 00:05:40.310
- Bundle's a beautiful word.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:41.143
(audience laughing)

00:05:41.143 --> 00:05:42.450
So it's, it's cool.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:43.650
And Bass Pros, our partner,

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:45.870
you usually do it through big box retail.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:48.000
And they're one of three
of the big boxes out there.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.100
But the other two big box retailers,

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.320
just their music section
just keeps shrinking,

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:53.430
shrinking, shrinking down.

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:54.960
And this one we got to help

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.450
Johnny Morris and Ducks
Unlimited to work on

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:59.490
conservation of wildlife
with this box set.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.516
- Oh wow.
- So it's a cool marriage.

00:06:01.516 --> 00:06:03.338
So that's why we're here
together. (audience applauding)

00:06:03.338 --> 00:06:04.171
- Beautiful.

00:06:04.171 --> 00:06:05.460
Well I love that

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.139
Do you listen to your old stuff?

00:06:07.139 --> 00:06:08.100
Are you always, you know....

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.851
- Oh my God, I love me.

00:06:09.851 --> 00:06:11.850
- (laughing)
(audience laughing)

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:14.757
- I love, you're like, look
at this jam I did in 91.

00:06:15.823 --> 00:06:17.220
- I can't believe I just said that.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.690
Me and you, I'm getting way
too comfortable around here.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:19.860
- No, you know why though?

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:21.270
It's actually very beautiful

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.460
because I, there are
sometimes I will say this,

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:24.540
it's only because of the performance.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:25.680
There's some things I look back on.

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:27.270
I'm like, I did good on that one.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.430
Like I get and I get proud
and I do listen to it.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:31.470
I am a lot of my listens on....

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:33.240
It's because sometimes you do get really

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.440
proud of certain things you do.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:37.680
And oh my god, when we were
kids in Oklahoma, Texas,

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:39.450
it was our dream to
get to accomplish this.

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:40.283
So it's like..

00:06:40.283 --> 00:06:41.237
- Amen.

00:06:41.237 --> 00:06:42.360
- You don't wanna take advantage of that

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.220
and just like really
recognize the blessing.

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:45.060
So I get that.

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:46.800
- Yeah, maybe guys are luckier than girls.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.900
'cause girls are always harder
on themselves of course.

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.340
But guys keep it kind

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.870
of conversational, right?
(guitar strums)

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:53.970
So you can listen to the old stuff

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.920
and the old stuff isn't singing as much

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:58.091
as just tell me the story.

00:06:58.091 --> 00:06:58.924
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:06:58.924 --> 00:07:00.030
- So, so how was this residency?

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:01.963
Because I went to the last
one. This one was different.

00:07:01.963 --> 00:07:03.629
Yeah, you did a different
thing. How has it been?

00:07:03.629 --> 00:07:05.490
- So, you know Caesar's,
the stage is pretty wide

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:06.780
and it's pretty wide for a one man show,

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.740
no matter how much ground I cover,

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.410
it's, it's still wide kind of thing.

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:12.090
So what we did is we
put dinner tables out,

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:12.923
hung chandeliers

00:07:12.923 --> 00:07:13.756
- Love

00:07:13.756 --> 00:07:15.360
- And people are sitting
at those dinner tables,

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:18.810
but the people sitting at the
dinner tables are the band.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:20.670
- Oh, I love that.
- So if you want to play

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.290
George Strait's Amarillo by Morning,

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.210
then Jimmy Mattingly just
picks up his fiddle, comes over

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.770
and plays with you and
goes back, sits down,

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.762
they're drinking all night.
At the end of the night

00:07:27.762 --> 00:07:28.595
you'll see.
(Audience laughing)

00:07:28.595 --> 00:07:29.428
But something, then the whole

00:07:29.428 --> 00:07:30.940
band comes up and we play 'Friends.'

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:31.773
Or 'Callin' Baton Rouge,

00:07:31.773 --> 00:07:32.606
some of that stuff.

00:07:32.606 --> 00:07:33.439
So it's fun.

00:07:33.439 --> 00:07:34.950
- Do you need to change it up like that?

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:37.320
- Yeah, because we got
through with the stadium run.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:39.090
They say, how do you make it
bigger than the stadium run?

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:39.923
It's easy.

00:07:39.923 --> 00:07:40.756
You guys know this.

00:07:40.756 --> 00:07:43.020
Flip it on its head where
it's just me and you

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.169
and the music.

00:07:44.169 --> 00:07:45.002
- Intimacy.

00:07:45.002 --> 00:07:46.813
- That's when it gets big,
right? (audience applauding)

00:07:46.813 --> 00:07:47.646
So cool.

00:07:48.839 --> 00:07:50.220
And here's the cool thing
that people are kind

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:52.440
of a little bit odd about at first.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:54.180
We bag the phones.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:55.846
- Oh yeah, yeah yeah.
- So you bag the phones.

00:07:55.846 --> 00:07:56.858
So you go in there.

00:07:56.858 --> 00:07:58.050
So we've had people come in and,

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:59.670
and you get emails and letters and,

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:01.650
and little sweet notes that go.

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:02.850
We came in and we sat down

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.040
and some people sat down, we didn't know.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.480
And you know what we did?

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:08.377
We started talking to them.

00:08:08.377 --> 00:08:09.210
(audience laughing)

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:10.043
- Oh my gosh.

00:08:10.043 --> 00:08:10.876
- It was like, are you kidding me?

00:08:10.876 --> 00:08:11.709
- Who would've thought?

00:08:11.709 --> 00:08:12.542
- Then they exchanged numbers,

00:08:12.542 --> 00:08:13.470
they became best buddies.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.850
They sang the same songs together

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:16.350
but didn't know each
other before that night.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:18.240
To me, that's what music is.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:19.980
Music is the voice of gathering.

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:21.038
- Connections.

00:08:21.038 --> 00:08:22.170
- Right, 100%.

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:25.860
Music makes, I don't know,
music makes good of everything,

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:28.350
but I also think it's
the voice of hope for us

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:31.410
to end up being together as a whole unit.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.370
I love Music.

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:33.300
- Me too.

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.740
I heard that you were playing new stuff.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:35.739
- That's what you do.

00:08:35.739 --> 00:08:36.572
- Like there was on this album,

00:08:36.572 --> 00:08:38.220
you were playing that at the Vegas shows.

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:39.960
Which is so special for fans.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.460
- So when you bag the phones, then you can

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:42.537
try new stuff on 'em, right?

00:08:42.537 --> 00:08:44.220
And they don't know that they're coming in

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:45.330
thinking they're gonna have a good time.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:46.163
Oh God.

00:08:46.163 --> 00:08:46.996
It's amateur hour.

00:08:46.996 --> 00:08:47.850
Here we go.

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:50.730
And you play them something
that they've never heard.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.800
And I'm telling you, it's like a Polaroid.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:53.633
It's instant.

00:08:53.633 --> 00:08:55.620
You get, you get the instant you suck

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:57.390
or holy cow kind of thing,

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:58.223
Right?

00:08:58.223 --> 00:08:59.889
(audience laughing) So
you get I'm into that.

00:08:59.889 --> 00:09:01.079
Or like, oh, should I go to the bathroom?

00:09:01.079 --> 00:09:03.330
- (laughing)

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:04.980
Alright, well tell me about this song.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.270
It's St. Paul Minneapolis, right?

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.103
- Yeah.

00:09:07.103 --> 00:09:07.936
- You did that one in Vegas, right?

00:09:07.936 --> 00:09:11.010
- Yeah, and in parentheses
it says, 'A true story.'

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:11.843
- Oh, I love it.

00:09:11.843 --> 00:09:12.750
So this really happened to me.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:15.150
- I mean, tell me about the
story. So you ran into someone.

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:15.983
- Yeah.

00:09:15.983 --> 00:09:17.490
And you can't tell much
because I really want this

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:18.780
person to tell me.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.420
So this person knows everything.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:22.530
But I gotta tell you

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.000
that it was something just really,

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.800
me and Miss Yearwood, we talk about it,

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:26.640
we take walks

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:29.880
and there was something so
easy about the conversation.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:30.870
It was crazy.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:34.080
So like, I just like to
find this person again

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.590
to see if, if it was something
that's always that way.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:38.423
And if it is, I wanna know why it...

00:09:38.423 --> 00:09:40.742
- Is it just something they
do. Or is it just (indistinct)

00:09:40.742 --> 00:09:41.575
- I have no idea.

00:09:41.575 --> 00:09:43.050
It, you know those
things you can't control.

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:43.883
- Yeah.

00:09:43.883 --> 00:09:45.407
- Those feelings that come over you.

00:09:45.407 --> 00:09:47.820
But I would love to see if I
could find this person and,

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:49.260
and just become friends.

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:52.440
She was, she was a great help

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.000
and a great period of time

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:56.550
and didn't ask for anything

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.710
or seem to assume anything in return.

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:00.000
- Oh my gosh.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.833
- It's good.

00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:03.767
- I Wanna find this person.
(audience applauding)

00:10:03.767 --> 00:10:04.996
Ah, because I want the whole story.

00:10:04.996 --> 00:10:06.510
(laughing)

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:08.130
Alright, well let's take a quick break

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:09.750
and grab some tissues.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:12.660
The Garth Brooks plus
one residency returns

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:15.810
to the Coliseum at Caesar's
Palace starting November 29th.

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:17.913
Go online for ticket information.

